      "prompt": "Design one coherent implementable Minecraft T1 thermal controller family concept sheet, five single-block controllers viewed slightly from above/front, all same block scale. Tesla lifetime late nineteenth-century practical industry. Image1 is material/style reference only: bold readable iron and restrained functional brass. Image2 is Smithy's EXISTING assembly context, not to redesign. Machines: 1 KILN: resource-pack gray cobblestone cube with large arched cast iron firing door, simple brick-shaped embossed mark and tiny lower ember slit. 2 FOUNDRY: red brick cube, sturdy square iron door with big simple pouring-crucible silhouette embossed on upper panel, lower ember inspection slot. 3 COOKING STOVE: dark cast iron cube with broad oven window/door, short brass horizontal handle, two large circular cooktop plates on top; compact loaf silhouette above door as secondary mark. 4 FERTILIZER FURNACE: warm copper cube with round sealed iron process door and simple readable two-leaf sprout stamp, small lower fire slit. 5 SMITHY CONTROLLER: red brick cube with compact iron ash/draft gate, big plain anvil emblem upper half and three broad horizontal lower vent slots; this controller sits underneath existing open forge, no extra burner. Existing 1-block footprints; no geometry changes to multiblocks, chimneys or machinery. Each purpose recognizable at Minecraft 32x block resolution from broad shapes, not microdetail. Restrained iron/copper wear, calm substantial surfaces, brass only handles/latches. One readable family, not five identical gauges. No pressure gauges, ornamental gears, text labels, loose items, futuristic screens, glossy plastic or fine filigree. Show hardware clearly, medium charcoal rather than black crush; neutral even lighting on plain background. Modest orange only inside lit fire slits, all outside surfaces normally shaded.\n",
